{"author":{"id":"673e1e1b6fccff4da5524407c8a8cdc7caf18221aabb93f2bb36ffef5c2a95e8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1781331244,"nonce":"G4ukPyEwgmTzcMtExsb5WQrmXlE=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOSn4-Gc8AAAABFW8oaw","github-url":"https://github.com/kanya-approve/karpenter-provider-rackspace-spot/issues/16","origin":"github"},"title":"Error classification by substring is fragile against the SDK's error wrapping","message":"`isAlreadyExists` / `isNotFound` classify SDK errors by string-matching, but spot-go-sdk rewrites HTTP errors into prose that doesn't always contain the tokens we look for.\n\n### Evidence\n- Our matchers: `pkg/providers/instance/instance.go:431-453` check `\"AlreadyExists\"` / `\"already exists\"` / `\" 409 \"` and `\"NotFound\"` / `\"not found\"` / `\" 404 \"`.\n- SDK `handleAPIError` (`spot-go-sdk@v0.2.0/api/v1/client.go:122`) maps:\n  - `409 Conflict` → `\"invalid request: \u003cbody\u003e\"` — **never contains `\" 409 \"`**, so that branch is dead; idempotent-create only works if the webhook body happens to include \"already exists\".\n  - `404` → `\"\u003cresourceType\u003e '\u003cname\u003e' not found\"` — matches `\"not found\"`, OK.\n  - `400 Bad Request` → `\"invalid request: \u003cbody\u003e\"` — a body like `\"server class X not found in region\"` would make `isNotFound` **misfire**, turning a validation error into a spurious NodeClaimNotFound.\n\n### Impact\n- Idempotent pool re-create on retry can break if the 409 body wording changes.\n- A 400 mentioning \"not found\" can be silently swallowed as NodeClaimNotFound.\n\n### Suggested fix\n- Match on the SDK's typed error: `errors.As(err, **HTTPStatusError)` and switch on `StatusCode` (409/404/400) instead of substring-matching prose.\n- Note: the in-code comment points to #4 for this, but #4 (closed) was scoped to rate-limit/quota, not error typing — hence this dedicated issue.","files":null}]}